comment.narrative:
The Cabinet of Ministers of Ukraine adopted Resolution No. 1049 dated October 03, 2023 "On implementation of the experimental project on the introduction of the comprehensive social service of resilience building" ("the Resolution") that approved the proposal from the Ministry of Social Policy to implement an experimental project on the introduction of the comprehensive social service of resilience building (the Experimental Project) during the period from October 7, 2023 to December 31, 2024 within the limits of budget allocations for the relevant period under the budget program 2501530 "Social protection of people in difficult life circumstances".
This resolution establishes that:
â€¢ the objective of the experimental project implementation  is to determine the content, scope, and procedure for delivery of the comprehensive social service of resilience building (the comprehensive social service);
â€¢ the coordinator of the experimental project and its spending agency is the Ministry of Social Policy;
â€¢ the participant of the experimental project, responsible for organization of a competition among social service providers, for contracting the comprehensive social service to social service providers based on the results of such a competition, and for paying for the services rendered, is the Fund for Social Protection of Disabled Persons ("the Fund");
â€¢ other participants of the experimental project are territorial communities.

The Resolution has approved:
1. Procedure for implementation of the experimental project on introduction of the the comprehensive social service of resilience building ("the Procedure for implementation of the experimental project").
2. The procedure for using the funds envisaged in the state budget for the implementation of the experimental project on introduction of the the comprehensive social service of resilience building.
The procedure for the experimental project implementation defines, inter alia:
â€¢ a list of activities that make up the content of the the comprehensive social service, classified in accordance with the following areas: needs assessment and determination of the road map for the the comprehensive social service recipient; delivery of psychological support to find internal and external personal resources and psychological assistance in presence of signs of psychological trauma, acute stress reactions and disorders caused by traumatic events; development of new behavioral models of adaptation for psychological recovery; education system, including interdisciplinary education, etc.;
â€¢ the procedure for carrying out the competition among social service providers, which establishes: a) phases of the competition; b) composition, procedure of establishment and operation for the competition committee; c) procedure for consideration of documents for participation in the competition; d) procedure for proposals evaluation in accordance with the pre-determined evaluation criteria for professional level, financial status, experience, etc.; e) drawing up a ranking list of proposals; e) publication of the competition results by the Fund;
â€¢ a mechanism for monitoring and reporting on delivery of the comprehensive social service of resilience building. During the experimental project, the main tasks of the comprehensive service provider are as follows: planning and coordination of specialists activities; monitoring of the comprehensive social service delivery by specialists; organization of document keeping regarding delivery of the the comprehensive social service, in particular, to ensure entering of information about the the comprehensive social service recipients into the Register of social services providers and recipients; interaction with the participants of the experimental project on the organization of the comprehensive social service delivery in the territorial community; preparation of monthly reports on the the comprehensive social service delivery to the authorized bodies of the Fund;
â€¢ the procedure of payment for the delivered comprehensive social service. In particular, the Fund shall pay for the comprehensive social service delivery on the basis of reports submitted by its providers about the comprehensive social service delivered in the reporting period (on a monthly basis), using the form approved by the MoSP's Order  dated October 13,2023, in accordance with the contracts signed through transfer cashless money to the accounts of the comprehensive social service the providers shown in their contracts, within the limits of the monthly budget allocations envisaged for implementation of the experimental project in corresponding budget period.
As on December 1, 2023, more than 20 territorial communities have been selected to participate in the experimental project, and the competitive proposals received from social service providers are being processed.

